            "review_title": "Review at Tau Saigon",
            "review_text": "tryagain M\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam57 contributions\n0\nSave your money, run away\nAug 2013 • Business\nWow..I brought my work partners and girlfriend there, hoping to show them the nice Vietnamese food, with entertaining Vietnamese music, on the quiet Saigon river. I've never been so wrong.\nWe were seated on the table just in front of the small stage, and were quiet exited about it. what a huge mistake. When the \"band\" arrived and started to play, we immediately understood that we had to leave. fast. The entire band had the same facial expression that we expect you to have at a funeral, and their \"music\" ( more like random noises) sounds like a End-of-the-year nursery school show. \n\"cerise sur le gateau\" as our french friend use to say, the special treat was the stinky water from the river, giving everybody nausea while trying to eat the poor quality food served.\nI almost forgot: we were at the first floor, closest from the water (bad, baaaad choice), and we could hear the music from the superior floor, in addition to the one from our floor, already non-bearable .\nall the food arrived at the same time, and everything was way below average, except the fish that was actually quiet good. we reached the boat at around 7:00, realized our mistake at 7:03, finished our food by 7:45, and left at 7:47, before the boat even had time to leave the harbor. \nWe just couldn't stand it longer. everybody had a huge headache and felt released to be away from this experience. \nNobody knows what happens afterlife. well, if you ask me, that's what Hell looks and feels like.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten August 6, 2013",
